# forjd-ui is the source of UI primitives

Suite law: `docs/SUITE_UI_UNIFICATION.md` — `--fj-*` must match DEML Viking-UI (void + electric `#2176ff` + gold). forjd-ui is an adapter, not a second design system.

Layout contract: `frontend/libs/forjd-ui/src/lib/README.md` — feature groups (`core`, `chrome`, `forms`, `overlay`, `feedback`, `data`, `layout`, `styles`).
Component APIs / usage: `frontend/libs/forjd-ui/COMPONENTS.md`. CSS twins: `src/lib/styles/SUITE_COMPONENTS.md`.

When adding a **component** or **typography** style to the frontend app, add it to `frontend/libs/forjd-ui/` in the same change (or immediately before the app consumes it). Do not leave reusable UI only in `frontend/src/`.

## What belongs in forjd-ui
- Standalone Angular components used (or likely reused) across routes/pages
- Buttons, inputs, badges, layout shells, and other primitives
- Typography scales, text styles, and shared type tokens (prefer `--fj-*` / library SCSS)
- Shared visual patterns that are not page-specific composition

## What may stay in the app
- Route/page shells and feature composition that wire library primitives together
- One-off layout that is clearly single-page and not a reusable control
- App-only data wiring, stores, and API clients under `src/app/core/` (not inside components)

## App presentation vs logic (landing)
- **Presentation:** `landing/landing.ts` + `.html` — signals and forjd-ui bindings only
- **Content:** `landing/landing.content.ts` — static copy / suite link builders
- **Use cases / infra:** `core/ready/` (single-slot probe cache), `core/monitoring/`, `core/bootstrap/`
- **State:** local component `signal` + `computed`; no multi-key global stores; theme/toast remain justified root services
- **Never** put `fetch`, readiness protocol, or monitoring DSN assembly in components or forjd-ui
- Layer table: `frontend/src/app/README.md`
- ADR: `docs/adr/0006-landing-layers-suite-adapter.md`

If unsure whether something is reusable, put it in forjd-ui.

## Required checklist (same change set)
1. Create the primitive under `frontend/libs/forjd-ui/src/lib/<group>/<name>/` (e.g. `forms/button`, `overlay/dialog`).
2. Export it from `frontend/libs/forjd-ui/src/public-api.ts` in the matching section.
3. Document selector + props in `frontend/libs/forjd-ui/COMPONENTS.md` (and CSS row in `SUITE_COMPONENTS.md` when chrome is new).
4. Add a colocated `*.stories.ts` Storybook story (+ JSDoc on non-obvious inputs/outputs).
5. Consume it from the app via the library public API — do not deep-import `lib/...` paths.
6. Prefer suite tokens (`--suite-*` / `--fj-*`) over ad-hoc colors/type in new styles.
7. Do **not** relocate `lib/styles/` (sync:suite + purity lockstep).

## Naming
- Selectors: `forjd-*` · Classes/types: `Fj*` · Files: `lib/<group>/<name>/<name>.ts`
- Services: `*.service.ts` · Specs/stories colocated (group-level stories OK)
- Tones: `FjTone` (not `VikingTone` in forjd-ui)
- UID: import `forjdUid` from `core/a11y/uid` (field-a11y stays pure)

## Import organization (in-file)
1. `@angular/*`  2. third-party  3. cross-group relatives  4. local `./`
- Blank line between blocks; prefer `import type` for type-only symbols

## Import boundaries
- `core/` must not import Angular feature groups (integration specs live under the feature group)
- Feature groups may import `core/` and documented peers (see `lib/README.md`)
- App → `forjd-ui` public API only
- Prefer shared helpers in `core/a11y/` (`NativeDialogSession`, `createToastStore`, `forjdUid`, roving/focus) over copy-paste in overlay/form components — keep dual Angular adapters; do not invent a shared npm package across DEML/FORJD

## Examples

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — new button only in the app
// frontend/src/app/shared/my-button.ts

// ✅ GOOD — primitive in library group, app imports barrel
// frontend/libs/forjd-ui/src/lib/forms/button/button.ts
// frontend/libs/forjd-ui/src/public-api.ts → export { FjButton } ...
// app template: <forjd-button>...</forjd-button>
```

```scss
// ❌ BAD — app-only heading scale for reusable type
// frontend/src/styles/_headings.scss (used across pages)

// ✅ GOOD — typography tokens/styles in forjd-ui, app imports library styles
```
